What to choose during investigation
Mode dropdown: rules (instant, deterministic — good for demos of the safety net), spring-ai or langchain4j (live Claude, ~10–60 s). Try the same sample in two modes — the output schema is identical, that's the framework-parity point.
Nothing else to fill — the plan is generated automatically and shown on the investigation tab.
What to do at review (same for every case)
Start review → UNDER_REVIEW
Skim Evidence + Citations tabs
Pick the disposition matching the table above; the only "clever" ones:
REROUTE — pick a different route from the dropdown (use it once to show the reviewer isn't a rubber stamp)
REQUEST_INFORMATION — routes to MANUAL_REVIEW when you think the missing info is disqualifying (e.g. the timeout case)
Write ≥15 chars of rationale referencing why (evidence/policy IDs score well in the audit)
Tick all 3 checkboxes — the missing-info one blocks submission when gaps exist
Optional second submission CLOSE → CLOSED
